                <pb facs="0438" n="373" sameAs="frus:frus1936v03/pg373"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.48 Mehabad/1: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Iran</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Merriam</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Teheran</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-08-07T12:00:00+03:25">August 7,
                        1936—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received August 7—9:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>48. Unprecedented flood has occurred at Mehabad (formerly Saujbulak) causing
                    destruction of 500 houses and the loss of more than 25 lives. American lives and
                    property there believed, safe. Also a severe earthquake has shaken Tabriz.
                    Americans there are safe but extent of the damage if any to mission property is
                    unknown at present. Recently there have been serious floods and earthquakes in
                    several parts of the country. The Shah has personally contributed substantial
                    relief funds.</p>
                <p>Improved atmosphere now observable, would be strengthened by a direct telegram of
                    friendly sympathy from the President to His Majesty. So far as I am aware thus
                    far no chief of state has so acted. No allusion shall be made directly or
                    indirectly to the American missions at the localities above mentioned.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Merriam</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
